test_connect_2d -- 2D connect: offsets, exact Delaunay, convex hull
(Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_connect_2d_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     12 decks, about 5 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IS TESTED

  connect on a triplane mesh object (2D Delaunay triangulation) of the
  same 400 points, made by make_connect_inputs.py from a fixed random
  number generator, in a 100 x 80 rectangle:

  cd01_origin      a corner at the origin: the reference
  cd02_utm         moved to x 4.0e5, y 3.9e6 (UTM-sized coordinates)
  cd03_negative    moved to x -6.5e5, y -4.2e6
  cd04_y_only      moved to y 3.9e6 only (x starts at 0)
  cd05_yz_plane    in the plane x = 0, moved to y 2.0e5, z 3.0e5
  cd06_xz_plane    in the plane y = 0, moved to x 2.0e5, z 3.0e5
  cd07_square1000  the four corners of a unit square at x = 1000 (the
                   case test/level01/connect_errors records as failing)
  cd08_graded      400 points crowded toward one corner ((u**3, v**3)
                   * 100): sizes over many orders
  cd09_stretched   a 31 x 31 grid 1000 long and 1 high
  cd10_jitter      a 31 x 31 grid of the unit square, every point moved
                   by up to 1e-9 (round-off in points meant to lie on the
                   sides)
  cd11_rings       a centre point and 10 rings of equally spaced points
                   (many cocircular sets)
  cd12_old_order   the cd08 points with connect / old_order (insert in
                   the order of LaGriT V3.3.4, not BRIO): must give
                   exactly the cd08 triangles

  HARD checks, every deck: LaGriT finished with no ERROR; connect left
  no point unconnected; the expected number of triangles (778; 2 for
  cd07); every triangle with positive area and the same orientation in
  its plane; every edge shared by one or two triangles; every vertex
  used. cd02-cd06 must also give exactly the triangles of cd01_origin,
  vertex number for vertex number.

  For every deck that reads a point file (all but cd07), checked with
  the full-precision coordinates of that file (the AVS dump keeps only
  13 digits) in exact rational arithmetic:
    Delaunay   no interior edge has the opposite vertex strictly inside
               the circle of the triangle on its other side
    hull gap   (convex hull area - mesh area) / hull area, at most 1e-6
               (connect leaves out only hull corners flatter than 1e-6)
  The 400-point decks must have 783 triangles = 2n - 2 - h for n = 400
  points with h = 15 on the hull: the whole hull. cd10_jitter must have
  no angle below 40 degrees (no slivers along the sides).

WHY

  connect (2D) starts from a large triangle enclosing the points
  (src/make_bigtri_lg.f). In LaGriT V3.3.4 and earlier its third vertex
  was placed at 1.01 times the centre coordinate of the points. Far from
  the origin that is far outside the box (4,000 m away for a 100 m box
  at x = 400,000), the triangle no longer encloses the points, every
  point fails and connect makes no triangles. Now the old place is kept
  when the box of the points contains the origin, so those meshes are
  unchanged, and otherwise the vertex is offset by 0.005 of the box
  size.

  The insertion tested whether a point is inside a triangle's circle
  against a fixed tolerance in area units, 2 x 3.25e-10 x (longest side
  of the box)**2, the same for every triangle. Small triangles could be
  left out of the insertion cavity although the point was well inside
  their circle (the mesh was then not Delaunay; connect ran recon / 0
  to repair it), and on a stretched box every test with the short
  spacing looked degenerate, so points were left out. For points in a
  coordinate plane the tests are now exact (lg_predicates2d.c: Shewchuk's
  error bounds, then double-double arithmetic when those do not decide).
  The triangles along the convex hull that the enclosing triangle
  displaced are added back and the mesh is flipped to Delaunay, exactly
  (lg_connect2d_hull.c).

  On LaGriT V3.3.4 and earlier, cd02, cd03, cd05, cd06 and cd07 make no
  triangles; the 400-point meshes miss 5 hull triangles; cd08 misses
  part of its hull; cd09 leaves 37 points out; cd10 and cd11 are not
  exactly Delaunay.

FILES

  make_connect_inputs.py   writes cd01-cd06 .pts (AVS points) into WORK
  cd*.lgi                  the decks
  check_connect_2d.py      the checker (Python 3, standard library)
  run_connect_2d_tests.sh  the runner; work/ and logs/ are rewritten
